Z||000002||fropuff||12-22-2001||05:52 PM||||Oil goes every 3000 miles (5000 kms?) and my plugs go 40-50K miles.  You need to quit changing oil and play with your little white dancing friend.  He looks lonely.<P>BTW: I meant the thing in his sig, for all the sick-minded folks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-22-2001||06:02 PM||||You cant change oil too often, I change my synthetic 2 times a year, spring and fall. Regardless of miles. plugs every spring. <P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-22-2001||06:21 PM||||Unless you drive 3000miles or it's metric equivalent every month, that is way too often. Traditional oil change interval for "severe service" is 6mo/3000miles. whichever comes up first.<P>Plugs, every month... that's just not right... plugs every year at the max unless you are buring allot of oil. Most good brands of regular plugs easily last 3 years. platinum types even longer.<P>Using "high test" in a car that doesn't need it just wastes money. It won't help and can actually hurt both performance and fuel economy. Most Fiero will run perfectly on 89 oct fuel. (Using U.S. fuel standards...) <P>The only reason to run more octain is if the motor pings. (Which is common in the 87-88 4 cylinder due to the way the PROM is programmed. GM pushed some timing points up a tad too far. There are PROM's that should correct that...) <P>Stop using STP and just use synthetic. I prefer Mobil 1 but use which ever you like. In most cases, you actually degrade the synthetic by adding things to it. Most additives are in a crude oil carrier. <P>Again, unless you are driving a huge number of miles, dropping the tranny pan every year is a waste. Dexron III is considered by GM to be a very long lasting oil. Even in these old TH125's the Dexron III fluid should last a long time. several years at least. (I forget the exact spec.)<P>Changing fluids too often usually won't hurt the motor/tranny but it's not good either. You spend way more money than you need to and generate far more waste. The oil is now recycled in many places now but the rest is all landfill.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||12-22-2001||06:35 PM||||i change my oil, every 3000 months or usually 3-4 months.<P>Maybe 1 or 2 times a year, ill pull the plugs out.  Thats only to clean them, and regap them to specs.  The gap usually doesn't change on me, when i look at the plugs.<P><BR>I would only change the oil every month if i was driving 3000 miles, or live in a dusty condition.  Otherwise, your wasting your money on oil, and filters.  Plus, its just another waste for the environment.  Refining oil, recycling etc...||||reg||1
